<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n30665" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nĕgātīvus</span></b> , a,
			um, adj.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>that denies, negative</i> (post-class. for negans, privans,
			etc.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">negativa actio,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Gai. Inst. 4, 3</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">particula,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">App. Dogm. Plat. 3, p. 32, 36</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">verba,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Dig. 50, 16, 237</span></i>
			; opp. confirmativus, Schol. <i><span class="en">Juv. 6,
			457</span></i>; <i><span class="en">14,
			127</span></i>.—Hence, adv.: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nĕgātīvē</span></b> , <i>negatively</i> (opp. affirmative),
					<i><span class="en">Cassiod. Dial. p. 548</span></i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense5"><b>(a).</b>; Boëth. ap.
				<i><span class="en">Cic. Top. 5, p. 359, 9</span></i> Bait.</div>
